Subject: [PATCH 0/2] arm64: dts: qcom: Add Milos CAMSS and FP6 ultra-wide
 camera support

This DTS-only series adds the Milos camera subsystem and enables the
Fairphone 6 ultra-wide camera.

Patch 1 provides the reusable SoC description: CAMSS resources, four CSI
input ports and the default MCLK1 pin configuration. CAMSS remains
disabled, with supply connections and sensor endpoints left to the board.

Patch 2 enables the FP6 OV13B10 and focus VCM, connects the sensor to
CSIPHY1, and supplies the board-specific power and pin configuration. The
OV13B10 reset state belongs to the FP6 board, not the common SoC include.
Sensor data lanes are numbered 1 through 4; the CSIPHY endpoint retains
its hardware lane indices 0 through 3. No unused MCLK1 sleep state or
unrelated camera support is introduced.

Binding dependencies, submitted separately to the media tree:
- Patch 1 requires "media: dt-bindings: camss: Add qcom,milos-camss".
- Patch 2 additionally requires "media: dt-bindings: ovti,ov08x40: Add
  OV13B10".
- The DW9714 binding is already upstream.

These patches apply to the Qualcomm tree at the base-commit below. The two
new bindings they rely on are being merged via the media tree and are not
duplicated here, so dtbs_check will report undocumented compatibles until
those land; please coordinate the merge order. The CAMSS and OV13B10 driver
series are also required for the camera to function.

Host-side validation of the revision prepared on 2026-09-06:
- W=1 DTB builds for Fairphone FP6 and Nothing Asteroids on the base and
  after each patch; existing DTC warnings were unchanged.
- CAMSS, OV13B10 and DW9714 schema checks with the prerequisite bindings,
  including explicit compatible matching and topology checks.
- Disabled, endpoint-free CAMSS at the SoC-only stage; sensor, lens and
  reciprocal CSIPHY1 connection after the FP6 patch.
- The FP6 patch left the Nothing Asteroids DTB byte-identical.
- Strict checkpatch on both patches: no errors, warnings or checks.

New upstream clock-controller power-domain and required-OPP properties
are retained. Earlier temporary Milos 7.2 testing exercised the camera
path, but used the historical DTS revision, including its old sensor
lane numbering. It is not boot validation of this updated DTS/base.

Thanks to Jorijn van der Graaf for the suggestions reflected in both patches.

